# Build 28: on the live AWS box one natural ~2.2 s lull between accepted
# perp aggTrades flipped EF to SPOT_FALLBACK while both lanes were live and
# the 5 s trade count was fine.  The trade-freshness limit is now driven by
# the observed inter-arrival cadence (bounded ring of accepted-trade gaps):
#   < MIN_SAMPLES gaps       -> STARTUP limit
#   otherwise                -> clamp(max(FLOOR, 1.5 * p99_gap + 250), FLOOR, CEILING)
# and a crossing of that limit alone gets a RECHECK_MS confirmation window
# before the source flips (new trade during the window keeps PERP).  Hard
# failures (lane down, depth stale, few levels, too few 5 s trades) never get
# grace.  Windows keep pruning against the current time: a 2 s lull still
# empties the 250 ms / 1 s deltas.  Not a strategy parameter.
